# Auto git commit + push

When all requested code changes in a turn/task are finished:

1. Create a git commit summarizing the work (follow the repo commit protocol: status, diff, log, staged files only, HEREDOC message, no secrets).
2. Push to `origin main` with a normal `git push` (not `--force` unless the user explicitly asks).
3. Do not ask the user to push; they will not run git push themselves.

Exceptions:
- Do not commit if there are no relevant changes.
- Do not force-push to main/master unless the user explicitly requests it.
- If push fails (auth/network), report the error and the local commit hash.
